connectome, which is released under CC-BY-4.0.

Cite the connectome paper when you use the pathway or a picture of it:

Berg et al., Cell, 2026. The male central nervous system of Drosophila
melanogaster. doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.015
https://male-cns.janelia.org/download/

The file keeps traced optic-lobe intrinsic neurons (lamina L1–L5 included),
visual projection neurons, and descending neurons. Edges are synapse counts
of at least 3 whose presynaptic transmitter has a signed consensus:
acetylcholine excitatory; GABA, glutamate, and histamine inhibitory.
Modulatory and unclear transmitters are dropped, not guessed. Photoreceptors,
central-brain intrinsic neurons, ventral-cord intrinsic neurons, and sensory
neurons outside the optic lobe are not in this file.

The closed loop follows the contract published by Fly.exe
(https://github.com/Ibtisam-Mohammad/Fly.exe): analytic vision, a shared
pathway with one neural state per vehicle, a 15 ms coupling, and a command
that is applied one interval later. Telotaxis does not copy that project's
source. The wheels, the onset timer, and the point-neuron step are
engineering, not measurements from the paper.
